# Every law this tree claims, with its verdict. One row per (law, subject): which law, which
# relation or instance, whether it holds, and the cardinalities or figures that decide it.
#
# A defect in the machinery
#   This is the relation examples/soundness/main.rs is a view of, and it answers a question
#   neither checks/ nor arithmetic/ asks. A check says the document contradicts the model. An
#   arithmetic site says you cannot compute here. This says the query does not compute what it
#   claims to: a defect in the machinery rather than in the evidence, and the only one of the
#   three that accuses nobody's filing. `conforms` is the one law about the evidence, and
#   algebra/roster.sqlc says why it sits here.
#
# The contract every law keeps
#   One plain SELECT, no leading WITH, returning exactly `(law, subject, holds, detail)`, with
#   `holds` NULL only on the roster row that found nothing to check. Same shape as checks/ and
#   arithmetic/, for the same reason: a law with an empty subject set must report as vacuous
#   rather than vanish from a GROUP BY. `law` is the roster's `slug` and not its formula, because
#   several laws share one formula.
-- algebra/roster.sqlc joined to each law's own subjects.
:union(ALL algebra/dimension_use.sqlc,
           algebra/compose_decomposition.sqlc,
           algebra/decomposition.sqlc,
           algebra/cycle_space.sqlc,
           algebra/composition_kernel.sqlc,
           algebra/composition_row_space.sqlc,
           algebra/composition_image.sqlc,
           algebra/composition_closure.sqlc,
           algebra/layer_units.sqlc,
           algebra/owed_equality.sqlc,
